    explanation: bi('Parity requires a domain symmetric about zero. On such a domain, even means f(−x) = f(x) for every input and gives reflection in the vertical axis; odd means f(−x) = −f(x) and gives symmetry about the origin. In the projection model, x² is even on R but not on [0, 3], because −1 is missing when 1 is allowed. The paper’s x² + 1 example is another even function on R, proved by its own identity. The punctured domain of 1/x is symmetric, so it can be odd without being defined at zero. The zero function satisfies both identities. On a symmetric domain, a function that is both odd and even has f(x) = −f(x), hence f(x) = 0 everywhere.', '奇偶性要求定義域關於零對稱。在這樣的定義域內，每個輸入均有 f(−x)＝f(x) 才是偶函數，圖像關於縱軸對稱；每個輸入均有 f(−x)＝−f(x) 才是奇函數，圖像關於原點對稱。投影模型 x² 在 R 為偶函數，在 [0,3] 卻不是，因為 1 被允許而 −1 沒有。紙本 x²＋1 是 R 上另一個偶函數，須用它本身的恆等式證明。1/x 挖去零的定義域仍對稱，所以可為奇函數而不在零有定義。零函數同時符合兩式。在對稱定義域內，同時奇偶必有 f(x)＝−f(x)，即處處 f(x)＝0。'),
